out-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate following its deploy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. First rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 (mixed fleet). A second rollback attempt completed successfully; all three regions are now on v2.3.0, service is healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-ups: investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure (note v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging) and the orchestrator error that interrupted the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The incident creation timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was actually created to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JNCpADxHMwG5CDsHW4T8tY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The incident was created despite the timeout (INC-0001), so no retry is needed.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Rollback completed:** checkout-api is now on **v2.3.0** in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), healthy, with error rate down from 18% to ~0.2%.\n\n**Why v2.3.0:** It was the most recent release with a healthy production history. v2.3.1-rc was skipped \u2014 it was staging-only and unhealthy.\n\n**Note on the rollback:** The first attempt hit an orchestrator error and halted after us-east, briefly leaving a mixed fleet (us-east on v2.3.0, the other two on v2.3.1). A second attempt completed all regions successfully.\n\n**Incident opened:** **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api) \u2014 the `create_incident` call timed out, but I verified via `list_incidents` that it was actually created, so I did not r